{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recorded."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a query or an update visits a world’s entities, the world can’t be changed in other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ways: spawning or despawning an entity, or adding or removing a component, would disturb the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage being visited. Record such changes in a command buffer instead, and apply them with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" once the visit is over. The following example despawns every entity whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"health has run out:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 10))","","var commands = Commands()","for (entity, health) in world.query(Health.self) where health.current <= 0 {","    commands.despawn(entity)","}","world.apply(commands)","","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A command on an entity that is no longer live when it applies does nothing, so two commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that despawn the same entity are safe.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Naming Entities That Commands Will Spawn","anchor":"Naming-Entities-That-Commands-Will-Spawn","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns a placeholder handle for the entity it will create. Later commands in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same buffer can name that placeholder, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns the real handles of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entities it spawned, in the order their commands were recorded:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","var commands = Commands()","let ship = commands.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","let turret = commands.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 0))","commands.addChild(turret, to: ship)","","let spawned = world.apply(commands)","print(world.parent(of: spawned[1]) == spawned[0])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A placeholder stands for its entity only inside the buffer that returned it; the world holds no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity with that handle.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Commands from Systems","anchor":"Commands-from-Systems","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system running alongside others can’t apply commands itself, because applying them would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change entities the other systems are reading. It queues them with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead, and the schedule applies every queued buffer at the end of each wave of systems."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:11WorldModule8CommandsV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}],"symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Commands.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Commands.swift#L55"},"title":"Commands","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Creating a Command Buffer","anchor":"Creating-a-Command-Buffer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/init()"]},{"title":"Inspecting a Command Buffer","anchor":"Inspecting-a-Command-Buffer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/count","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/isEmpty"]},{"anchor":"Spawning-and-Despawning-Entities","title":"Spawning and Despawning Entities","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/clone(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/despawn(_:)"]},{"anchor":"Adding-and-Removing-Components","title":"Adding and Removing Components","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldMod